  "articleBody": "A well-prepared countertop replacement starts with documenting the existing kitchen, deciding whether the layout will stay, comparing materials by performance and maintenance, and requesting a detailed written scope. Have the installer take final field measurements, confirm every cutout and edge detail, and identify cabinet, plumbing, electrical, permit, demolition, and disposal issues before fabrication begins.",
